diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d532f62..28ad835 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,18 +3,33 @@
 A small command-line task tracker that stores tasks in a JSON file.
 
 ```
-tasker add [-p N] <title words...>     add a task (priority 1-5, default 3)
-tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority] list open tasks (or all)
+tasker add [-p N] [--tag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD] <title words...>
+                                                  add a task (priority 1-5,
+                                                  default 3; --tag repeatable)
+tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority|due] [--tag T] [--overdue]
+                                                  list open tasks (or all);
+                                                  --tag (repeatable) keeps only
+                                                  tasks having ALL given tags;
+                                                  --overdue keeps open tasks due
+                                                  before today; --sort due puts
+                                                  no-due tasks last
 tasker done <id>                        mark a task done
 tasker rm <id>                          delete a task
-tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T]     change priority or title
+tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T] [--tag T] [--untag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD|none]
+                                       change priority, title, tags or due date
+tasker tags                             print every tag used by open tasks
+                                        with its count, sorted by tag
 ```
 
+Tasks may carry tags (lower-case, `-` and digits) and an optional due date
+(`YYYY-MM-DD`, stored as UTC midnight). List lines show the due date and tags
+when present, e.g. `#4 [ ] P2 file taxes (due 2026-04-15) [home,money]`.
+
 The data file is `$TASKER_FILE` (default `tasks.json` in the current directory).
 
 ## Layout
 - `internal/model` — the Task type and validation.
-- `internal/store` — loading/saving the JSON file (with a schema `version`).
+- `internal/store` — loading/saving the JSON file (schema `version` 2; version-1 files load fine).
 - `internal/query` — filtering and sorting.
 - `internal/cli` — argument parsing, commands and output formatting. `cli.Run` is the testable entry point.
 - `cmd/tasker` — main.
